These contain NO Benro/Snoppa source and NO decompiled/reconstructed firmware
code. `stage2_patch.py`'s only Benro-specific data is the list of PUBLIC LGPL
libgphoto2 API names the stock binary calls (`gp_*` / `gp_port_*`) — names, not
code. The reliability-patch sites are discovered from the user's own binary's
symbol table at run time. The loader's three shims read/write only PUBLIC
libgphoto2 struct fields and call PUBLIC `gp_camera_set_config` /
`gp_camera_set_single_config` APIs — no firmware code.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
LGPL-2.1 (libgphoto2 — third party, rebuilt from source)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
The custom firmware image this tool WRITES (full mode) contains freshly-built
libgphoto2 binaries:

  libgphoto2.so.6          (core)
  libgphoto2_port.so.12    (port)
  ptp2.so                  (camlib)
  usb1.so                  (iolib)

These are Copyright their respective authors and are distributed under the GNU
Lesser General Public License, version 2.1. Corresponding source is the official
upstream release, rebuilt verbatim by this tool from:

  https://github.com/gphoto/libgphoto2/releases/tag/v2.5.34   (default; --libgphoto2)

There are exactly TWO documented source modifications, both applied to the
official upstream tree by this tool's own scripts, both adding NO proprietary or
firmware-derived content:

  1. ABI pad — a one-line `char _reserved_tail[4120];` appended to `struct _Camera`
     so the rebuilt core allocates the same Camera size the Benro binary expects.
     4120 is an interop SIZE constant, not Benro code; ABI-inert for the library
     (upstream never reads the tail). Applied by build_ptp2.sh (FULLSTACK=1).

  2. EOS-init error tolerance — `container/dbg_patch.py` (POLARIS_DBG=1) makes a
     handful of Canon EOS init-time event/keep-alive drains non-fatal
     (`camlibs/ptp2/config.c` check_eos_events ×13; `library.c` keep_device_on ×3
     + check_eos_events ×1): the transient non-OK each returns the first time is
     captured and discarded instead of aborting camera_init. It is a mechanical
     edit of upstream's own LGPL source (swap `C_PTP(x);` → `{ … = x; (void)…; }`),
     adds no new symbols or dependencies, and is a no-op when the camera returns
     OK. This is a modification OF the LGPL work and is offered as such.

The corresponding (modified) source is fully reconstructible: take the upstream
release above and run container/build_ptp2.sh / container/dbg_patch.py, both in
this repository. See docs/HOW-IT-WORKS.md and container/build_ptp2.sh.

When the tool runs in full mode it writes `out/licenses/` with the libgphoto2
`COPYING` (LGPL-2.1) and a source-offer note alongside the produced firmware, so
anyone redistributing the resulting image carries the required LGPL notice and
source pointer.

This project ships NO firmware and, in the repository itself, NO libgphoto2
binaries — they are built from source at run time. It is not affiliated with or
endorsed by Benro, Snoppa, Canon, or the gPhoto project.
